# ─── Secrets & personal data ──────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
app/.env

# Operator's filled-in investor one-pager. Contains personal financial info
# (income, family, residency). The .template stub is committed for new clones.
# Anchored to the repo root on purpose: an unanchored `philosophy.md` also
# matches `docs/philosophy.md`, which is the committed guide.
/philosophy.md

# Local Claude Code session/permission data
.claude/

# Dated one-off / cleanup scripts — leak specific tickers and trade dates.
# Kept on disk for personal reference; not for public consumption.
archive/

# Planning notes and prompt sources that are the operator's own working
# material rather than part of the project. `docs/` itself IS tracked — it
# holds the user-facing guides; only `docs/internal/` is excluded.
docs/internal/
.kombai/
Claude for Finance/

# PowerShell launchers and Task Scheduler wiring: host-specific, Windows-only,
# and superseded by the Makefile + compose. Untracked rather than deleted —
# they stay on disk on the operator's box, where live scheduled tasks still
# call them by path.
/run_*.ps1
/setup_*.ps1
/check_mcp.ps1

# Machine-specific compose deviations (data dir, ports, …).
# docker-compose.override.yml.example is the committed template.
docker-compose.override.yml

# Cached ticker logos enumerate the operator's holdings/watchlist. Fetched
# at runtime by app/fetch_ticker_logos.py; browser falls back to the CDN
# for symbols without a cached file.
app/dashboard/static/logos/

# ─── Postgres data ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only present when a bind mount is configured via an override; the committed
# compose keeps the database in the `pgdata` named volume.
data/

# ─── Generated / cached ───────────────────────────────────────
cache/
*.log
*.bak
*~

# ─── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
# coverage.py drops a SQLite db wherever it is run, and the two suites run from
# different working directories — so a single `pytest --cov` leaves one at the
# repo root and one in app/. Neither was ignored, so both were one `git add -A`
# away from being committed. coverage.xml is listed for the day SonarCloud
# coverage reporting gets wired up; it is the report that upload would consume.
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
dist/
build/
.venv/
venv/

# ─── IDE / OS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

#Ignore Understand Anything json config files
.understand-anything/

#Ignore vscode AI rules
.github/instructions/codacy.instructions.md

# Codacy CLI local tooling config / cache (generated by the CLI install)
.codacy/

# Exported design handoff (Open Design) used to build the modern dashboard.
# Source artifact, not part of the app; kept locally for reference.
Example/

# Scratch input doc for docs/plan.md — kept locally, not version-controlled.
suggestions.txt

# Local database dumps from `make backup` — copy them off this machine.
backups/

# Impeccable design tooling — PRODUCT.md / DESIGN.md capture product and visual
# context for AI-assisted design work, and .impeccable/ holds its config,
# detector suppressions and critique snapshots. Working notes for this machine,
# not part of the app or its published documentation.
PRODUCT.md
DESIGN.md
.impeccable/

# Agent-harness hook stub. Not a GitHub-native path — GitHub does not read
# .github/hooks/ — and the config is inert here: it guards on a vendored
# .github/skills/impeccable/ that this repo does not carry. The detector that
# actually runs is wired through the gitignored .claude/ settings.
.github/hooks/
